		class Item152
		{
			dataType="Comment";
			class PositionInfo
			{
				position[]={14823.538,17.91,16719.35};
			};
			title="Automatic Bar Gate";
			description="To create an automatic bar gate, simply copy the example one provided and past it into your mission. " \n "" \n "Then change the gate's variable name to something like gate3." \n "" \n "Then edit the trigger (the blue aura thing) and change the 'On Activation' and 'On Deactivation' portion to be the same name as the gate. " \n "" \n "Eg: The gate is named gate3" \n "" \n "It should say in the 'On Activation' section;" \n "" \n "gate3 animate [""Door_1_rot"", 1] " \n "" \n "and in the 'On Deactivation' section;" \n "" \n "gate3 animate [""Door_1_rot"", 0] " \n "" \n "And you're done!";
			id=1265;
		};
		class Item153
		{
			dataType="Comment";
			class PositionInfo
			{
				position[]={14805.564,17.91,16704.623};
			};
			title="Custom Spawn Location";
			description="~~~ OBSOLETE ~~~" \n "Unless for a very particular situaion, you will use the new 'Respawn at height' method. " \n "" \n "The script is already in the mission template files. All you need to do is the following. " \n "" \n "player setPosASL getPosASL respawn_can; " \n "" \n "- Place the respawn_west marker as usual.  " \n "" \n "- Place an object on the deck of the ship or at the height you want the respawn to be. The object can be anything that is a solid object. I'd recommend something small and not easily noticeable. " \n "" \n "- Turn of damage and simulation on the object. " \n "" \n "- Name the object: respawn_can" \n "" \n "- Test it and you're done.";
			id=1266;
		};
